 ],
 "literal": "Cloud-reached rising rain hill's / waterfall-filled cool fragrant glory lily / buds having blossomed ceaselessly smelling fragrant forehead, / many-petalled cool eyes, O dark-skinned woman! / Whether you agree or whether you kill, / you, having measured, know your greatness; like truth, / speaking false words, why is that? / The heart is good indeed on your side!",
 "translation": "O dark-skinned woman with many-petalled cool eyes and a fragrant forehead that ceaselessly smells of the cool, sweet glory lily buds blossomed by the waterfalls of the rain-swept hills where clouds gather! Whether you accept him or whether you kill him, you know your own greatness after weighing it. Why then do you speak false words as if they were the truth? His heart is truly good and devoted to you.",
 "modern": "மேகங்கள் சூழ்ந்து எழுகின்ற மழையைப் பொழியும் மலையின் அருவி நீரால் நனைந்து, மலர்ந்த குளிர்ந்த நறுமணமிக்க செங்காந்தள் மொட்டுகளின் ஓயாத நறுமணம் வீசும் நெற்றியையும், பல இதழ்களைக் கொண்ட குளிர்ந்த கண்களையும் உடைய மாஅயோளே! நீ தலைவனை ஏற்றுக்கொண்டாலும் சரி, அல்லது அவனைக் கொன்றாலும் சரி, உன்னுடைய பெருமையை நீயே ஆராய்ந்து அறிவாய். உண்மை போலப் பொய்ம்மொழிகளைக் கூறுவது ஏனோ? அவனுடைய நெஞ்சம் உன்னிடத்தே மிகவும் நல்லதாகவே இருக்கிறது.",
 "explanation": "In this Kuriñci poem, the heroine's close friend (thozhi) speaks to the heroine (thalaivi) who is feigning indifference or anger toward the hero. The friend describes the heroine's beauty using the rich imagery of the mountain landscape, where glory lily buds are nourished by waterfalls on rain-swept hills. She points out that whether the heroine decides to accept the hero's love or reject him (which would be like killing him), she must act with the dignity and greatness that define her. The friend questions why the heroine speaks false words of rejection when her heart is actually filled with love. Ultimately, she reassures the heroine that the hero's heart is entirely good and devoted to her.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
